    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 22 at 5:48AM PDT until October 22 at 8:45AM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "* WHAT...Urban area and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of Eastern Los Angeles County in southwestern\nCalifornia...\n\n* WHEN...Until 845 AM PDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nWater over roadways.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 547 AM PDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain due to thunderstorms. This  will cause urban and small\nstream flooding. Up to 1 inch of rain has fallen.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nPomona, San Dimas, Glendora, La Verne, Claremont, Diamond Bar and\nWalnut.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
